cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pulp, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pulp: Grind a local folder into one LLM-ready dump"
abstract: >-
  Pulp walks a local folder, extracts the text from source code, PDFs,
  Office documents, notebooks, and archives in parallel, and writes a single
  plain-text, Markdown, or XML file to hand a large language model. It runs
  on the user's machine, from the command line, a localhost web interface,
  or a WebAssembly build in the browser, and uploads nothing.
authors:
  - family-names: Gass
    given-names: Bryan
    alias: BeeGass
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BeeGass/pulp"
url: "https://pulp.onlygass.dev"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - text extraction
  - document conversion
  - command-line tool
  - rust
  - webassembly
